 the candidate is accepted. T1 and S1 stops are unchanged, except that T1 comet and S1 harbour now carry the interchange marks.","T2 stops in line order from (306,320): parade z 30, harbourside z -290, docks z -600 (all at x 306), comet (-50,-726), then lantern z -575, rocket z -265 and terraces z 200 (all at x -334). Gaps along the track, counting the r50 fillet as 78.5 m in place of 100: 320, 310, ~461, ~427, 310 and 465 m. All are inside 300–500.","Each 30 m platform is on straight track. Docks (-615 to -585) ends before the corner tangent at z -676. Comet (x -65 to -35) sits between the T1 flat crossing (Boulevard edge at x -14) and the tangent at x -296. Lantern (-590 to -560) starts after the Sunset shift ends at about z -590. Terraces (185 to 215) ends before the Crown Road fillet at z 236.","Reach for the four plots that failed: harbour-east 50 m (to harbourside), docks-east 98 m (to docks), rocket-west 80 m (to rocket), lantern-west 75 m (to lantern). Terraces brings crown-terraces from 247 m down to about 172 m. All other plots were already inside 222 m.","Interchanges: T2/parade (306,30) to S1/harbour (290,0) is 34 m. T2/comet (-50,-726) to T1/comet (0,-688) is 63 m. Both are under 150. T1, S1 and T2 now form one connected network (N-C1).","Fronts (W-3): T2 stops sit 6 m from the centrelines of 24 m primary roads, inside the carriageway (Harbour Road x 300, Comet Row z -720, Sunset Way x -340). Roads are walkable, so W-2 holds.","Mismatch with Datum's ask: it puts S1 Harbour at (340,0), but the station is at (290,0) in both the candidate and my stops. The pairing works either way. Also still open for Aster: notes/why describes the old draft and contradicts notes/concept."],"sources":["7dfdfdf13043a24e8e964b0b","538618090dd534247cab5493","ba506de42600790962a866a2","8753ed1758ca27e6cf152279","0e426f4211a2f1f25c328968","e20799f1f673824d09ce452d"],"answers":[{"from":"Datum","ask":"Place T2 Harbour Line stops, 300–500 m apart, on straight track. Cover harbour-